test_restart_pg_after_error reads get_error() on the non-zero ranks once,
after a fixed 4 s sleep. The REMOTE_ERROR propagated from rank 0 can arrive
just after that (measured 3.96 s to 4.06 s with the NCCL bundled in the
2.10.0 wheels), so the test fails intermittently. Poll for the error with a
deadline instead.

Author: Rohit Goswami (SURF)

--- a/test/distributed/test_c10d_nccl.py
+++ b/test/distributed/test_c10d_nccl.py
@@ -4009,6 +4009,15 @@
             # other ranks not exiting before rank 0 timeout, this is to avoid
             # nccl error happening before rank 0 timeouts
             time.sleep(4)
+            # The remote error arrives once rank 0 has timed out and propagated
+            # it, which can be just after the fixed sleep. Poll for it instead
+            # of reading it once.
+            deadline = time.monotonic() + 60
+            while (
+                nccl_backend.get_error() == ErrorType.SUCCESS
+                and time.monotonic() < deadline
+            ):
+                time.sleep(0.1)
             self.assertEqual(nccl_backend.get_error(), ErrorType.REMOTE_ERROR)
             new_file_name = store.get("file").decode()
 
